'''NOPW Wednesday Episode 9''' was the ninth weekly [[Wednesday Night Wrestling|Wednesday night]] professional wrestling event produced by [[New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling|NOPW]], held on August 19, 2026 at the Toyozawa Municipal Gymnasium in [[Toyozawa]], Okaiken's second-largest city. The show was the G1 fall-out finale and the launch of the [[G1 Climax 2026]]: the tournament field and block draw were announced live, headlined by the main event of [[Marcus Vance]] defeating [[Nakamura Shinsuke]] in 21 minutes — and by the draw itself, which placed the champion and the workhorse in the same block.

== Background ==

One week after [[Leoni Masua]] announced his G1 entry at [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 8|Episode 8]], NOPW gathered its full roster in Toyozawa for the block draw. The storylines entering the show:

* '''Vance's silence,''' now two weeks old, had become the loudest thing in the company. His opponent, Nakamura Shinsuke, had promised to "make the silent man scream."
* '''Kengo's freefall''' — two straight losses, a mutinous faction, and a block placement still to come.
* '''The television title.''' Yuto Ono, the 10-day champion, had never defended the gold. Tadayoshi Ishida, his Seigigun stablemate, had asked for the match himself: "The young lion carries the belt. The man carries the responsibility. I will take both."
* '''The makeshift junior challengers.''' Tetsuya Yamamoto and Akira Sato, closing the gap on the junior tag champions with every challenge.

