== Match details ==

* '''Match 1:''' Iwata's roll continued — the cutter on El Phantasma at 10:18, the young lion's fourth win in five weeks. '''Crowd:''' '''IWATA''' chants. HEAT for the Phantom's mask games.
* '''Match 2:''' Malo against the first Uso — the singles run rolling through the twins one at a time. Tama's timing made it close; Malo's power ended it at 12:51. '''Crowd:''' '''MALO''' chants. HEAT when Riku ran in for the save attempt and ate a double clothesline.
* '''Match 3:''' The makeshift challengers' latest shot — and the closest yet. Yamamoto's flash pins nearly stole it twice before the Flash Flood on Sato at 13:24. The champions retain; the gap keeps closing. '''Crowd:''' dueling chants. Respect applause for the challengers.
* '''Match 4:''' KAZUKI's tune-up, and the calm before six weeks of war. The Twin Star Press on Morita at 11:09. '''Crowd:''' '''KAZUKI''' chants.
* '''Match 5:''' Kengo's makeshift Cannon Club — himself and Tanaka, the last two men willing — against the tag champions. Reyes and Kimura's second defense ended Kengo's night again: the Cobra Clutch on Tanaka at 14:32. '''Crowd:''' NUCLEAR HEAT for Kengo. '''COBRA''' chants.
* '''Match 6:''' The television title. The 10-day champion against the man who asked for the match. Ono's speed and belief against Ishida's patience and leg — and it was the veteran's night: the Ishida Lock at 16:47, center ring, the young lion tapping in his first defense. Ishida is the new World Television Champion. Handshake after — the guard did not pass, but it was coming. '''Crowd:''' '''ISHIDA''' chants. Respect for Ono, who raised the new champion's hand himself.
* '''Match 7:''' The main event. Nakamura had promised to make the silent man scream — instead, the silent man made the King of Strong Style tap the mat in frustration and take the Drill Driver clean at 21:00. Vance's second silent win in six days broke the clip record set at Episode 8. He said nothing, again. '''Crowd:''' '''VANCE''' chants throughout. STANDING OVATION at the finish — the loudest sound the silence ever made.

== The block draw ==

After the main event, the full G1 Climax 2026 field gathered on the stage for the live draw:

* '''Block A:''' [[Leoni Masua|Leoni]], [[Marcus Vance|Vance]], [[Kawada Masahiro|Kawada]], [[Ryohei Maeda|Maeda]], [[The Marauder|Marauder]], [[Honda Masanori|Honda]] (the AOPW representative — the first outside wrestler in G1 history), [[Nakamura Shinsuke|Nakamura]], [[Kengo Vaiahi|Kengo]], [[Big Stan|Stan]], [[Katsuhiko Morita|Morita]].
* '''Block B:''' [[KAZUKI (wrestler)|KAZUKI]], [[Takagi Yuto|Takagi]], [[Taumafa Vaiahi|Taumafa]], [[Jusuf Muntasir|Jusuf]], [[Daigo Kuroki|Kuroki]], [[Tadayoshi Ishida|Ishida]], [[Yuto Ono|Ono]], [[Mamadou Diallo|Diallo]], [[Jin Tanaka|Tanaka]], [[Diego Reyes|Reyes]].

The draw's detonations, in order: '''Leoni and Vance in the same block''' — the most anticipated G1 block match in a decade, scheduled for Round 5 in Naruto. '''Kengo in Block A with Leoni, Vance, and Big Stan''' — the man who betrayed the family, the man he excommunicated, and the giant who walked out on him. '''Jusuf in Block B with KAZUKI, Takagi, and Taumafa''' — the truth-teller against the block's entire top shelf.

KAZUKI, asked for a comment on the draw, gave the line that defined his tournament: ''"I have been one before. I will be one again."''

'''Crowd:''' ERUPTION at the Leoni–Vance placement. '''G1''' chants to close the show.

== Storyline notes ==

* '''The record broken twice in a week.''' Vance's silent walk at Episode 8 became the most shared clip in NOPW Wednesday history; the Nakamura win at Episode 9 passed it within 24 hours — 12 million views.
* '''Ishida takes the television title.''' The new champion enters the G1 — where Day 2 in Okami would bring the 8:56 that changed his tournament. Ono enters having just lost the gold, the guard unpassed but closing.
* '''Kengo's block is a death sentence.''' ''Tokuyama Sports'' called the draw exactly that. Three men with reason to destroy him, nine matches to survive.
* '''The Wednesday series pauses.''' With the G1 tour running September 5 through October 18, NOPW Wednesday went on hiatus after this show, returning at [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 10|Episode 10]] on October 14.

